# Never commit a database dump/backup accidentally (two such files, full application exports including
# credentials tables, were committed by mistake on 2024-02-05 and later removed from the tree - see
# commits 74fb7931f/717f4d9e1; they remain in git history, which is a separate, explicit cleanup this
# rule does not address). The tracked schema-only file db.sql is the one intentional exception.
# Also block the common compressed/renamed variants of an ad-hoc dump (a dated history scan (M7,
# 2026-10-27) additionally found a stray 45-byte pittpc.tar.gz from 2019 and two docker/.env files
# from 2023, all already absent from HEAD - these patterns stop that class of mistake going forward).
*.sql
!/db.sql
*.sql.bak
*.sql.gz
*.sql.zip
*.dump
*.tar.gz
!/vendor/**/*.tar.gz
.env
docker/.env
docker/**/.env
!.env.example

